// The control center's browser API (docs/design.md §3.3, §3.4, §8, §10).
//
// Served with Connect under /api on the control center. Browsers call it with
// @connectrpc/connect-web (Connect protocol, JSON or binary).
//
// Authentication is a session cookie ("swarm_session"). Every unary call must
// carry the Connect protocol header "Connect-Protocol-Version: 1" (connect-web
// sends it) and, if the browser sends an Origin header, it must match the
// control center's own origin; that is the CSRF protection. Server streams
// need the cookie only and change nothing.
//
// Sign-in with OIDC and SAML is a browser redirect, not an RPC:
//   GET  /auth/oidc/{provider}/login?return=/path
//   GET  /auth/oidc/{provider}/callback
//   GET  /auth/saml/{provider}/login?return=/path
//   POST /auth/saml/{provider}/acs
